Z||000000||MISTER_PORKY||09-17-2001||04:49 PM||||HI FOLKS !<BR>   DOES ANYONE KNOW WHERE I CAN HAVE A VEHICLE IDENTIFICATION NUMBER CHECKED TO SEE IF A CAR IS AN AUTHENTIC FACTORY T-TOP ?<BR>    THANKS FOR ANY HELP !<P>GOD BLESS NEW YORK, AND ALL OF AMERICA !||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||09-17-2001||06:05 PM||||Welcome!  Far as I know the only really TTops were made in 88.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||09-17-2001||06:37 PM||||Check on the RPO sticker it should have the CJB code for the t-tops.  The sticker is in the front trunk.  This was only onthe 88's||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||09-17-2001||06:37 PM||||Look at the rpo code sticker on the inside front fender. You should have a CJB code if it,s an 88. <BR>there is also a site called T-Top Registry (I don't have the address handy but it,s easy to find in a search)that you can put in the VIN number and they will verify it as well as send you some neat information, original dealer, Date of conversion, the cars number in order of conversion and a sticker facsimile. listing all accessories and price..||||reg||1
Z||000004||MISTER_PORKY||09-17-2001||10:21 PM||||O.K.<BR>   Several people have gotten on to me for typing in all caps. I work in an engineering office and I type in all caps there. Have been doing it for aver 20 years. I'll try to break old habits.<BR>    Anyway, thanks for the info. I am familiar with the t-top registry. I didn't realize I could find out there though. I was also told yesterday by a dealer that t-tops were offered in "86 - '88 Fieros. However, I'm interested in an '88gt T-top only. From what Ive been finding, if I want a low milage mint/near mint car, I'm going to have to spend some pennies ! <BR>    Thanks again for the help folks !<P>GOD bless the U.S.A.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||09-18-2001||08:01 AM||||Finally someone that has heard the truth. Yes they was offered by dealers in 86. Mine was fitted with them by the dealer in 86. Not a factory option, but by some dealers ahead of the times. Yet they get shunned over cars with a little factory option sticker on them. Go figure hey.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||6
